v1.2 changes (vs v1.1):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FEATURE — Repeating / scheduled tasks ("set it and forget it"):
     - Two NEW optional per-task fields, both ADDITIVE and absent by default, so
       legacy tasks are unchanged (NO migration) and the kids' board files stay
       byte-identical:
         * `repeat`     : { every:int>=1, unit:"hours"|"days"|"weeks" }
         * `startUntil` : ISO-8601 "available from" (past/absent = show now).
     - A task can be a ONE-TIME FUTURE task (hidden until startUntil arrives, e.g.
       "buy milk tomorrow") OR a RECURRING task (e.g. "empty dishwasher" every day).
     - Spawn on complete (SERVER-SIDE, authoritative): in api.php's PATCH handler,
       when a task carrying a `repeat` spec transitions into Completed, a fresh,
       INDEPENDENT Pending copy is appended (same title/description/duration/
       repeat) with startUntil = completed_at + every*unit. It is written in the
       SAME atomic save as the parent (both persist together), is UNASSIGNED by
       design (each occurrence is a fresh claim for the kids), and the response
       carries a `spawned` field so the UI can acknowledge it. A one-time task
       (no repeat) spawns nothing.
     - Rescheduling: a Pending task's startUntil / repeat can be changed via PATCH;
       it is LOCKED once the task has started (same Pending-only rule as content
       edits — a non-Pending reschedule returns 403).
     - UI (admin.html): one quiet "Schedule" control, COLLAPSED by default
       ("None" = create now, no repeat). Tapping it reveals two rows — "Available
       from" (datetime-local, defaults to now) and a Repeat toggle (Every [n]
       [hour/day/week], off by default). Only sent to the server when meaningful,
       so a plain task gains neither key. Edit mode prepopulates both from the
       task; add mode resets to defaults.
     - UI (index.html): the Pending filter skips tasks whose startUntil is still in
       the future; a small "↻ N{h/d/w}" chip renders on cards that carry a repeat
       spec so a recurring chore reads as recurring at a glance.
     - Timezone story: the browser converts the local datetime-local value to a UTC
       ISO string before sending; the server stores everything in UTC 'c' format
       (matching created/completed/started) and computes the next occurrence from
       completed_at + delta. No offset drift.
     - Verified on the dev server (24/24 automated checks on a throwaway `scratch` board,
       then removed): plain task gains no keys; future startUntil hidden / past
       shown; a completed repeating task spawns an UNASSIGNED copy at
       completed_at+1h that persists; a one-time completion spawns nothing;
       rescheduling a non-Pending task -> 403. Kids' boards left byte-identical.

  BUG FIX 1 — Completed tasks: owner is locked:
     A task's owner (assignee) can no longer be changed once the task is Completed.
     - api.php: a PATCH that sets `assignee` is refused (HTTP 403, "owner locked —
       a completed task's owner cannot be changed") when the task's ORIGINAL status
       is Completed — including a combined "move out of Completed + reassign in the
       same request" (the check reads the pre-mutation status, so it can't slip
       past). A refused change is rejected before the board is saved (no trace).
     - index.html: a Completed task shows its owner as a 🔒 locked tag; tapping it
       does nothing (the reassign picker won't open). Pending/InProgress/Halted can
       still be reassigned freely, just like a card move.
     - admin.html: already safe — its edit form only opens for Pending tasks.
     - css/style.css: new .assignee.locked (frozen look).
     - Verified on the dev server: reassign / unassign / combined-move on a completed task
       -> 403; reassign on a Pending task -> 200.

  BUG FIX 2 — Completed tasks cannot be deleted:
     A task that is Completed is permanent and cannot be deleted.
     - api.php: a DELETE is refused (HTTP 403, "cannot delete — a completed task is
       locked and permanent") when the task's status is Completed, checked before
       any mutation.
     - index.html: a Completed task's delete ✕ renders as a 🔒 lock and the click
       is refused; deleteTask() also guards it client-side.
     - admin.html: the row delete renders as a 🔒 lock for Completed tasks; the
       delete handler is only wired for non-locked rows.
     - css/style.css: the delete ✕ and the owner tag on a completed card share the
       SAME 🔒 lock, unified into one rule (not-allowed cursor, --muted color,
       opacity .55, 14px, 2px 5px) -> new .del.locked / .mini-del.locked.
     - Verified on the dev server: delete a completed task (URL + body forms) -> 403;
       delete a Pending task -> 200; kids' board data untouched.

  COSMETIC (folded in during this release, no version of its own):
     - Fixed the "Schedule" section chevron: it was rendering a literal "\u25be"
       (a JS escape in the HTML body) instead of a triangle; swapped to the HTML
       entity &#x25BE; so it renders as a real ▾ and still rotates 180° on open.
     - Kept the repeat spec ("1 / every / [unit]") on ONE line: wrapped the number +
       "every" + unit dropdown in a .repeat-spec group so the unit dropdown no
       longer wraps to a second line.
     - Removed the stray "All tasks" section from the admin add/edit page: it was a
       second .panel rendering a live task list that no longer belonged there and
       was throwing "Can't find variable: n" (a ${n} in the renderer that should
       have been t.duration). The section + its loadList() machinery were removed
       and replaced by a tiny config-only loader so the add/edit form still
       populates its duration/assignee dropdowns on a plain add.

